&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Value Marketing Manager&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team:&lt;/strong&gt; Marketing – Business Value Services · &lt;strong&gt;Reports to:&lt;/strong&gt; Head of Business Value Services · &lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; San Francisco&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Sigma&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sigma is the cloud analytics platform built directly on the data warehouse. Business teams use it to explore live data with the ease of a spreadsheet and to build interactive data apps on top of Snowflake, Databricks, and BigQuery, with AI now doing a growing share of the work. We crossed $200M in ARR and raised an $80M Series E at a $3B valuation, and we are growing fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is &lt;strong&gt;value marketing&lt;/strong&gt;, owned by Business Value Services: turning the outcomes customers have already realized into proof the go-to-market team uses to win and expand accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our Business Value Marketing Manager, you&#39;ll own how the value customers realize with Sigma becomes proof the whole go-to-market team can use. You&#39;ll build the system that tells us which customers are seeing results and why, then turn those outcomes into a steady supply of published proof and reference-ready advocates that sales and Business Value Services can pull from to win and expand accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an individual-contributor role and an entry point into marketing at Sigma.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The value-proof engine &lt;/strong&gt;Build and run the system that turns customer outcomes into published proof on a predictable cadence: case studies, videos, and quote cards grounded in real outcome data. This role turns customer outcomes into proof &lt;em&gt;for&lt;/em&gt; prospects, the market, and the sales team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advocacy and references &lt;/strong&gt;Grow a referenceable-customer bench relevant to our field sales teams, run the advocacy program, and feed Majors and ABM with proof tied to the value a customer has already realized.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Value stories at events &lt;/strong&gt;Source and prepare customer speakers for our biggest annual events such as Snowflake Summit, Databricks DAIS, and our own Workflow conference. Own the Sigma User Meetups (SUMs) webinar series.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reviews and recognition &lt;/strong&gt;Drive review volume and quality on G2 and Gartner Peer Insights, and run programs like &quot;Built with Sigma&quot; awards that give customers a reason to put their name next to ours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Customer Advisory Board &lt;/strong&gt;Own and mature Sigma’s CAB program in partnership with Business Value Services, and turn what you hear into both product input and pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Distribution of Resources&lt;/strong&gt; Bring relevant stories into the website, the sales plays, and the ABM pages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The agentic stack &lt;/strong&gt;Operate the AI-first system (Sigma, Claude, and the connected tooling) so drafting, repurposing, and distribution run at a volume one person plus agents can sustain, and improve that system as you go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Three to five years in B2B SaaS value marketing, customer advocacy, customer reference, customer success, BVS, or a closely related field. This is an entry point into marketing, so adjacent experience counts.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of creating proof and references yourself, not only executing an existing playbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong writing and storytelling instinct, and the judgment to find the one outcome in a customer conversation that a prospect will actually care about.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with AI tooling. You have built, or are eager to build, agentic workflows, and you are not precious about doing by hand what an agent can do better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data fluency. You can work inside a warehouse-native analytics product, pull your own outcome numbers, and partner with RevOps without needing everything handed to you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Event and customer-speaker exposure, and the diplomacy to manage customer relationships and executive stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A cross-functional operator who works across sales, Business Value Services, customer success, product marketing, and field marketing without friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Job details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this position is $126 - 148k annually.&lt;/p&gt;
