&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Head of Pipeline Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sigma Computing is looking for a Head of Pipeline Strategy to build and optimize the internal systems that power our GTM teams&#39; pipeline generation. This role owns the analytical foundation of our sales plays: TAM/SAM profiling, signal identification, and performance measurement, ensuring every play we build actually drives the pipeline and ARR outcomes we&#39;re targeting. You&#39;ll partner closely with Sales, Business Development, Marketing, and Product, and report to the Global Manager of GTM Enablement. Based in San Francisco or New York.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own TAM/SAM profiling and signal identification, ensuring plays target the right accounts, personas, and buying signals, and tie directly to pipeline and ARR outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the analytical backbone for GTM programs: track message efficacy, conversion rates, and rep performance to guide what changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure program and campaign impact through rigorous reporting, using data to continuously refine plays rather than just report on them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead a Pipeline Generation program with Sales, Business Development, Marketing, and Product, delivering field assets against targeted use cases and verticals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify timely GTM campaign opportunities using data and market insight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project manage cross-functionally to pull together what a strong pipeline program requires&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with SMEs to define new sales plays for emerging product areas, plus the supporting assets (decks, sequences, discovery questions, call scripts)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think like an analyst first, comfortable owning TAM/SAM sizing, signal identification, and performance measurement, and you use data to prove whether a play is actually working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve operated as a program manager, pulling together Sales, Marketing, and Product toward a shared goal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in sales enablement, revenue operations, GTM engineering, marketing, or related roles, ideally with complex technical sales cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert with AI, data, and the GTM tech stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Business, Marketing, or related field preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt; Occasional travel between SF, NY, London, and Sydney offices, plus conferences/workshops as needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By joining Sigma Computing, you’ll be stepping into a transformative role that will shape the sales trajectory of our organization. If you&#39;re ready to spearhead change and drive unparalleled sales performance, we&#39;re eager to meet you.&lt;/p&gt;
