&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Sales Compensation Manager is vital for scaling and operationalizing Sigma&#39;s sales compensation process. You will ensure accurate, timely compensation payouts using expert analysis and refine processes, tools, and reporting to align compensation with business results. This role is ideal for a self-starter who thrives on ownership, data integrity, and cross-functional collaboration between Finance, Revenue Operations, and GTM leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Commission &amp;amp; Incentive Processing&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute end-to-end commission calculation validation and processing for sales commissions and incentive payouts with high accuracy and precision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, troubleshoot, and resolve calculation discrepancies and stakeholder escalations efficiently. Support compensation accruals and roll-up reporting in coordination with Finance close cycles.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Systems &amp;amp; Platform Administration&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage Sigma’s compensation platform with the broader team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead system updates, user access coordination and UAT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure clean data flows between CRM (Salesforce), HRIS, ERP, and comp systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Plan Governance &amp;amp; Communication&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support administration of quota rules, crediting structures, and payout policies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare clear plan documentation, and communication for GTM teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Finance, Sales Operations, HR/People, and Data to align comp mechanics with business strategy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, prioritize, and implement process improvements that increase accuracy and reduce manual effort.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in sales compensation, ideally within fast-scaling SaaS orgs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency with Salesforce CRM, Sigma and spreadsheet tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with consumption-based models and usage-driven GTM strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail, robust problem-solving skills, and a strong systems mindset.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communication skills with the ability to clearly translate complex compensation logic for both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: Hands-on experience with modern sales comp tools (e.g. QuotaPath, CaptivateIQ or similar), including plan configuration, calculations, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Double Bonus: Working knowledge of SQL or comparable query languages for advanced commission modeling and troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
