&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;(Sr.) Revenue Accounting Manager&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sigma Computing is seeking a Senior Revenue Manager to join our Revenue team and play a key role in managing revenue accounting and revenue operations in a fast-growing SaaS environment. Reporting to the Senior Director of Revenue, this role will own key aspects of the revenue close, revenue recognition, contract review, and related processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Revenue Manager will serve as a subject-matter expert on revenue accounting, partnering closely with Sales, Deal Desk, Legal, FP&amp;amp;A, and Finance to assess complex customer arrangements, ensure appropriate revenue treatment, and build scalable processes and controls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own key components of the monthly, quarterly, and annual revenue close, including revenue recognition, deferred revenue, unbilled revenue, and related reconciliations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with ASC 606 and applicable accounting standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review customer contracts and non-standard arrangements to determine appropriate revenue recognition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales, Deal Desk, Legal, FP&amp;amp;A, and Finance to assess the accounting implications of new products, pricing structures, and complex deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and approve revenue-related journal entries, reconciliations, and supporting schedules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, maintain, and improve revenue accounting policies, procedures, and internal controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own accurate and timely billing operations, including review and validation of sales tax applied to customer invoices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own sales tax compliance processes, including periodic reviews of nexus, taxability, and potential exposure across applicable jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal and external audits, including preparation of revenue-related schedules and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to streamline, automate, and scale revenue processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance Systems and other stakeholders on revenue system enhancements and process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the implementation and optimization of revenue-related functionality within NetSuite and other systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide analysis and insights to the Senior Director of Revenue and broader Finance leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a subject-matter expert and resource for the broader Finance organization on revenue recognition matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and support other members of the Revenue team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6–10+ years of accounting experience, including significant revenue accounting experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of ASC 606 and revenue recognition principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex customer contracts and revenue arrangements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of month-end and quarter-end close processes, reconciliations, and internal controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively in a cross-functional and fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a SaaS / subscription-based technology company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of SaaS revenue models, including subscription, usage-based, and professional services arrangements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with NetSuite, particularly SuiteBilling and revenue-related functionality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing, optimizing, or scaling revenue recognition processes and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CPA or equivalent accounting qualification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a high-growth technology environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
