&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Sr. Content Marketing Manager&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; San Francisco, CA · In-office 4 days/week &lt;strong&gt;Team:&lt;/strong&gt; Strategic Marketing &lt;strong&gt;Reports to:&lt;/strong&gt; Sr. Director, Strategic Marketing&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sigma produces a lot of content — blog, video, product launches, thought leadership — and this role is the editorial backbone that makes all of it sharper, faster, and on brand. You&#39;ll run the Sigma blog end-to-end, raise the quality bar on everything that ships, and build the systems and internal bench that let us scale content without losing voice or accuracy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior, hands-on editorial role for someone who edits with both technical judgment and taste. You&#39;ll work shoulder-to-shoulder with PMs and engineers to keep content accurate, coach employees and contractors to produce great work, and bring new thinking to how Sigma earns awareness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join an established content team and won&#39;t have to do it all yourself — a Content Producer partners with you on publication and operations. This role reports to the Sr. Director of Strategic Marketing, with room to grow into people management as Sigma&#39;s content team scales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll own&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Editorial standards and editing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Edit a high volume of blog posts, balancing technical nuance with taste. You&#39;re comfortable editing in the data, analytics, apps, or AI space — you don&#39;t need to know everything, but you know what you don&#39;t know, flag it, and lean on PMs and engineers to keep content accurate and clear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep Sigma&#39;s content on brand across every channel and format.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reinforce the standards that contribute to great content: Clear positioning, high-quality imagery, and connected messages across multiple content pieces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Blog and AEO operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the Sigma blog end to end:&amp;nbsp; calendar, editorial standards, and publication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the AEO content calendar and the relationship with Sigma&#39;s AEO contractor, ensuring 5 AEO blogs are edited, SME-reviewed, and published each week. The team&#39;s Content Producer supports publication, with you staying hands-on in edits and reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enabling internal voices&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the content calendar and the system that enables employees to write thought leadership blogs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help PMs draft product content for the blog and social — providing guidance and editing — and build the bench of internal SMEs generating content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring fresh ideas for promoting new product features on LinkedIn and X.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive and thought leadership support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
